The Trigger Optimizer
"Profiling render loop performance and battery conservation:


   1. Unrestricted Continuous requestAnimationFrame Loop: Currently, render() schedules the next frame unconditionally via requestAnimationFrame(() => this.render()), even when !this.isWalking and not dragging, and even when the canvas is scrolled out of the viewport! The canvas recomputes 32 coil ellipses, multiple linear/radial gradients, and drop shadows on every frame.
   2. Stationary Equilibrium Resting-State Gating: When !this.isWalking && !this.isDragging, the engine should pause its animation loop once the coils settle, resuming immediately on launchWalk(), drag, or API triggers.
   3. IntersectionObserver Viewport Gating: Wrapping the canvas in an IntersectionObserver to pause rendering when scrolled out of view reduces idle background CPU usage to 0% on mobile Termux runtimes.
   4. OffscreenCanvas Background & Staircase Caching: The playroom linear gradient, brass beveled border, and 5-step wooden staircase with carpet runners are completely static. Pre-rendering them onto an internal stairsCacheCanvas once during resize() and copying them via a single ctx.drawImage() eliminates over 50% of per-frame canvas draw calls."
